Patch 2506: shadow comparisons lower the reference by a receiver-plane depth bias of SHADOW_RPDB shadow-map texels
(default 2, 0 = off); the constant shift of patch 2505 now defaults to 0.

The reference's change across the given number of shadow-map texels is worked out from its screen-space derivatives
together with the lookup's (capped at 0.05): large on surfaces at a grazing angle to the light, near zero on surfaces
facing it. Patch 2505's constant 0.02 removed J-Stars' self-shadow lines but cut away part of the ground shadow near
the feet (0.008 too); this keeps the lines away and most of that shadow. Still a workaround: the cause of the lines
is open (the v0.15 port and RPCS3 show neither).

Tested (US disc, attract demo watched at 1440p, High shadows): SHADOW_RPDB=2 no lines, a small gap near the feet;
=1 lines back. Free Battle 29.8 flips/s (bench/feature/2026-11-09_2047-rpdbdef).

diff --git a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
index 4b105414..f7ec2cb1 100644
--- a/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
+++ b/libs/video/rsx_fp_decompiler.c
@@ -512,15 +512,15 @@ u32 rsx_fp_texture_units(const u8* ucode, u32 max_bytes)
     return units;
